# In-process and working files, including the message a commit is given with
# -F. Gitignored so that naming it on the command line can never put it into
# the commit it describes.
.ephemera/

# Session entry point: ephemeral by design, rewritten each session.
START_HERE.md

# Python's caches. This repository's own Python went with the port; what is
# left is the checkers linked in from toolbox, which run from here and leave
# their caches here. Both entries carry a `.gitignore` holding `*` that the
# tool writes itself, so a cache hides from `git status` on its own account and
# these lines are belt to that brace.
__pycache__/

# Adopted jig links, and the run directories they produce. The links resolve
# into toolbox; in a built image the same files arrive from the anvil layer
# beneath, so a committed copy would be a third statement of one thing.
bolt.*.yaml
adapters/
.bolt-*/

# Adopted checker scripts, linked into bin/ from toolbox.
bin/*.py

.ruff_cache/

# The built binaries. bin/infobot and bin/forget-session are committed shims
# that exec these; an absent binary is reported rather than rendering blank,
# which is FR-1.13 and the reason the shims are the committed half.
bin/statusline
bin/forget
